<doctext field_name="doctext">I switched to [metamod://Marpa::R2] instad of [metamod://Parse::RecDescent]. I had to change the grammar a bit to make it work:
&lt;c&gt;
#!/usr/bin/perl
use warnings;
use strict;

use Marpa::R2;
use Data::Dumper;

my $dsl = &lt;&lt; '__DSL__';
:default ::= action =&gt; [values]
lexeme default = latm =&gt; 1

seq     ::= '(' seqstrs ')'
seqstrs ::= seqstr seqstrs | seqstr
seqstr  ::= seq | tagstr
tagstr  ::= OZN seq | OZN rijec

OZN      ~ [A-Z.,?'*:`]+
rijec    ~ [\w\-?,:&lt;*`*]+
space    ~ [\s]+
:discard ~ space
__DSL__

my $grammar = 'Marpa::R2::Scanless::G'-&gt;new({ source =&gt; \$dsl });

my $input = "(SBARQ (WHNP (WP Who))(SQ (VP (VBZ says)(, ,)(S (SBAR (`` ``)(IN If)(S (NP (PRP you))(VP (VBP do)(RB n&lt;t)(VP (VB look)(ADJP (JJ good)))))(, ,)(S (NP (PRP we))(VP (VBP do)(RB n&lt;t)(VP (VB look)(ADJP (JJ good)('' &lt;&lt;)))))))))(? ?))";

my $result = $grammar-&gt;parse(\$input);
print Dumper($result);
&lt;/c&gt;&lt;P&gt;

It seems you confused &lt;C&gt;(&lt;/C&gt; and &lt;C&gt;'('&lt;/C&gt; . Marpa doesn't know the &lt;C&gt;(s)&lt;/C&gt; , you have to enumerate the alternatives.&lt;P&gt;

